<!--
  kuna constselectjump reentry: a dispatcher loop jumps through one register,
  and each step's code loads the next step's address and jumps back to the
  dispatch. Flow recovers the dispatch's first target before the code that
  re-enters it is decoded, so upstream keeps a one-entry table and drops every
  later step's store. P2 flow / switch-model; P0 assertion `option
  constselectjump`. Original GNU N32/N64 fixtures (tests/fixtures/
  indirect-dispatch/) dispatch through $31 (with returnbranch) and through
  ordinary $9, re-enter directly, before the dispatch, through a second
  indirect jump, and reach the caller's return early or through a conditional
  branch. Pass 1 (`off`) keeps only the first store; pass 2 (the default
  `reentry`) retries the dispatches the new edges reach and keeps every store,
  the loop and a defined default for the caller's return. The CLI companion
  indirect_dispatch.rs executes the emitted C against the stores at O0/O2.
-->
